		{
			"id": "112789446151269355",
			"parentId": "112789380092334286",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@Schepp/112789445849117768",
			"author": {
				"name": "Christian \"Schepp\" Schaefer",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@Schepp",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/294/814/597/449/022/original/cc8d1c1e842b92c6.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-15T07:59:22.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>nhoizey</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@cferdinandi\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cferdinandi</span></a></span> Here is the thread screenshotted. The bug report mentioned is this one: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41392507\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">issues.chromium.org/issues/413</span><span class=\"invisible\">92507</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112789632843380711",
			"parentId": "112789446151269355",
			"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey/112789632812455446",
			"author": {
				"name": "Nicolas Hoizey",
				"url": "https://mamot.fr/@nhoizey",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/230/453/300/889/original/b21203c65dbd197c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-15T08:46:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@Schepp\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>Schepp</span></a></span> thanks! 🙏</p><p>From what I read in the bug report, Pat Meenan said “it's not likely to work in practice for most origins where it's lucky if they even support prioritization at all”… 😞</p><p>So it looks like inlining critical CSS is important indeed, even more for large HTML documents.</p><p>But inlining CSS is complex and can be detrimental, as shown by <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://webperf.social/@csswizardry\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>csswizardry</span></a></span>: <a href=\"https://csswizardry.com/2022/09/critical-css-not-so-fast/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">csswizardry.com/2022/09/critic</span><span class=\"invisible\">al-css-not-so-fast/</span></a></p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@cferdinandi\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cferdinandi</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112789881123552481",
			"parentId": "112789632843380711",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@Schepp/112789881059146450",
			"author": {
